### Requesting Adjustments

At DLA Piper, we aim to make meaningful progress and build an inclusive culture where anyone affected by disability, neurodiversity or a long-term health condition has an equitable and accessible chance of success. If you think you may need adjustments or additional support to enable you to participate in our recruitment process, please contact our **Recruitment team** and we will be happy to support you.

### Agile Working

We recognise that people have responsibilities and interests outside of their career and that as a business, we all benefit from working flexibly. That’s why we are open to discussing with candidates the different ways in which we are able to support requests for agile working arrangements.

### Pre-Engagement Screening

In the event that we make an offer to you, and where local legislation permits, we will conduct pre-engagement screening checks that may include but are not limited to your professional and academic qualifications, your eligibility to work in the relevant jurisdiction, any criminal records, your financial stability, and references from previous employers.

## Our hiring approach

Our hiring approach enables us to learn about the professional and person you are, and gives you the opportunity to learn about us. Your recruitment experience can differ depending on the type of role you are interviewing for. You will always meet your direct Line Manager for your role, as well as peers and close collaborators for the position. For some of our roles we may also use assessment tools, practical exercises, and panel presentations. Your Recruitment Business Partner will inform you of the recruitment process at the start of any recruitment process, but please let us know if you have any questions prior to making an application.

Global Value Dossiers Consultant - Global Health Economics team - UK at IQVIA

Back to Jobs

# Global Value Dossiers Consultant - Global Health Economics team - UK

London, United Kingdom | Full time | Hybrid | R1573929

Apply Now

* Job Description
* Testimonials
* Culture
* Global Talent Network

**The team & the company**

IQVIA is a leading global provider of advanced analytics, technology solutions, and clinical research services to the life sciences industry. IQVIA creates intelligent connections across all aspects of healthcare through its analytics, transformative technology, big data resources and extensive domain expertise.

With direct access to the world’s most comprehensive healthcare information, analytics and research resources, IQVIA experts design and deliver innovative data– and technology-enabled evidence programs to accelerate the clinical development and commercialization of innovative medical treatments that improve healthcare outcomes for patients. IQVIA Global Health Economics is a fast-growing and highly successful consultancy business, focusing upon on delivering tangible business results to our clients who are key decision-makers and business managers across the international pharmaceutical and healthcare industry.

The IQVIA Global Health Economics team is composed of around 200 highly qualified multi-disciplinary professionals from a variety of disciplines including health economics, health technology assessment (HTA) strategy and evidence generation, based in 12 geographies, with projects delivered across >50 countries.

Our clients operate in the life sciences industry, including global top 20 pharmaceutical companies and biotech companies, as well as public health providers and regulatory authorities. They are looking for insight and evidence around the safety, efficacy, effectiveness and cost-effectiveness of health care delivery systems and pharmaceutical products spanning the full spectrum of therapeutic and disease areas. Our diverse mix of clients, the breadth of disease areas, as well as increasing access to novel data sources and methodologies provide a constant and rewarding challenge for our people.

For more information about our company please visit our website: https://www.iqvia.com/

**Role purpose**

This role will offer you the opportunity to support our Global Health Economics team as a Consultant Medical Writer and be part of our HTA Evidence & Strategy Centre of Excellence and Value Communications Centre of Excellence.

This role focusses on medical writing for health economic and outcome research (HEOR) and HTA purposes, where you will be responsible for writing tasks within projects and work with a senior team to co-manage small workstreams, project tasks and thought leadership initiatives.



Typical projects include medical writing for EU Joint Clinical Assessment (JCA) dossiers, HTA dossiers (predominantly NICE, SMC, NCPE), global value dossiers (GVDs), payer objection handlers, payer value stories/messaging, literature review protocols and reports, reports for evidence synthesis and health economic modelling studies, and HEOR-focused peer-review manuscripts and conference abstracts. The audience for the project deliverables will be various life-sciences customers as well as healthcare payers, providers, and regulators. You will work within a team of highly experienced health economists and outcomes research specialists providing support across a range of HEOR projects, working in a cross-functional and cross-country project team, providing medical writing, undertaking quality control, and contributing to the management of project delivery (including guiding and reviewing the work of more junior team members).



The role will expose the candidate to the broad range of payer-focused offerings in value communications, HTA strategy and HEOR to support in business development opportunities. An ideal candidate will have a good understanding of the matrix structure typical of our clients in the pharmaceutical industry and how to successfully navigate this structure to achieve clients’ aims. Furthermore, the candidate should demonstrate an ability to interpret clinical, economic and real-world evidence and translate findings into compelling value narratives and payer focused communication strategies to optimize a product’s access to markets and its reimbursement.

**Qualifications and Skills**

Extensive experience with medical writing in HEOR/HTA/payer materials is essential for the role. We are looking for proactive individuals with strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Candidates should have a strategic mindset, the ability to identify potential issues and suggest solutions. The ideal applicant should have strong interpersonal skills and the ability to establish relationships with both internal team members and clients. As such, fluency in conversational and business English and strong communication skills is essential. The ability to demonstrate clear scientific communication in English through slide deck development, report writing, and presentations is essential.

We recruit individuals from a variety of backgrounds to join our well-rounded team. If you are motivated, have a passion for healthcare, have strong organisational skills, and expertise in payer-focused medical writing we encourage you to apply. Key skills for this role include:

* Degree in life sciences (or related), epidemiology or health economics and policy, preferably a Master’s degree;
* Significant experience in medical writing across multiple therapeutic areas (~5 years, minimum 3 years HEOR/HTA experience specifically), including direct experience writing GVDs and/or benchmark HTA submissions (e.g., NICE or G-BA dossiers), peer-reviewed publications, and HEOR study reports/protocols;
* Experience managing and coordinating delivery of GVDs and/or benchmark HTA submissions, or parts of these deliverables;
* Familiarity with health economics and health technology assessment processes, ideally JCA, NICE or G-BA;
* Strong written and verbal English communication skills, expertise in scientific writing requirements;
* Ability to produce high-quality written content with minimal guidance from senior team lead;
* Excellent Microsoft office skills (expert in use of MS Word), and high attention to detail;
* Self-motivated with a strong desire to learn quickly and independently, ability to work autonomously with appropriate guidance when needed;
* Strong time-management and organisational skills, and flexibility to work in a fast-paced environment.

**Responsibilities**

* Independently produce high-quality written content for GVDs/HTA dossiers (JCA, NICE, and/or G-BA), HEOR study reports (e.g., SLR, NMA, ITC, modelling, secondary database research, manuscripts, conference abstracts, and other payer materials (e.g., objection handler, value story / value proposition development) with minimal guidance from project manager;
* Ability to collaborate effectively across multidisciplinary and geographically dispersed teams;
* Work with senior team to co-manage small projects or workstreams, project tasks and thought leadership initiatives (i.e., guide junior team members, first review junior team members output, client management);
* Conduct quality control reviews of HEOR documents and maintaining audit trails of changes;
* Mentor and train less experienced Medical Writers;
* Contribute to medical writing training initiatives to upskill the team and set quality standards;
* Support the team’s Centre of Excellence initiatives;
* Manage your own time and responsibilities to meet project requirements with clear communication with project managers, line manager and resource manager to ensure utilisation and compliance targets are met.



**Important**

* Please submit your CV in English.
* Please note that we don't provide any visa suport.

IQVIA is a leading global provider of clinical research services, commercial insights and healthcare intelligence to the life sciences and healthcare industries. We create intelligent connections to accelerate the development and commercialization of innovative medical treatments to help improve patient outcomes and population health worldwide. Learn more at https://jobs.iqvia.com

IQVIA is committed to integrity in our hiring process and maintains a zero tolerance policy for candidate fraud. All information and credentials submitted in your application must be truthful and complete. Any false statements, misrepresentations, or material omissions during the recruitment process will result in immediate disqualification of your application, or termination of employment if discovered later, in accordance with applicable law. We appreciate your honesty and professionalism.

## Where you'll work

### Hybrid

You’ll split your time between home and the office, giving you the flexibility to focus where you work best while still building strong in-person connections with your team. This model combines the autonomy of remote work with the collaboration, energy and resources of an office environment.

Vacancy

# Knowledge and Information Assistant

Apply for role



### We are recruiting a Knowledge and Information Assistant to join our Innovation & AI department on a part-time basis

## About Macfarlanes

Macfarlanes is a pre-eminent law firm that serves a global client base in Private Capital, Private Wealth, M&A and Disputes. Personal connection, an entrepreneurial spirit and a commitment to excellence are at the heart of our firm. These values drive our ability to deliver exceptional outcomes for our clients.

We are big enough to undertake the most complex and demanding mandates yet small enough to know each other well and to be agile, adapting to the needs of our clients. We seek to strengthen the firm by recruiting talented people from all backgrounds who want to build long-lasting and impactful careers with us. Our culture is challenging and supportive, creating an environment where individuals can thrive.

## What this means for you

Joining Macfarlanes means being part of a collaborative, approachable team who want you to succeed. You’ll be encouraged to get involved and recognised for your contribution.

We take your development seriously. Our learning and development programmes are second to none and are designed to help you strengthen your skills.

Above all, you’ll be part of a firm where we all work together as part of a cohesive and supportive team, value your efforts and help you to thrive.

## Role and background

The Knowledge and Information Services teams sit within the Knowledge and Data pillar in the Innovation & AI department, and supports the firm through knowledge, information, AI, and data technologies, working closely with Partners, Knowledge Lawyers and staff on knowledge sharing and collaboration initiatives. They are responsible for developing, maintaining and promoting our:

* firm’s culture of knowledge sharing and collaboration;
* knowledge management systems, related practices and processes, including ensuring compliance with GDPR and other relevant law and regulation;
* firm’s know-how and precedent collections, architecture and taxonomies;
* firm’s intranet and internal collaboration solutions;
* enterprise and legal search engines and associated AI integrations;
* firm's library, information resources and research services; and
* firm’s culture of knowledge sharing and collaboration.

We are looking for a proactive, collaborative and enthusiastic Knowledge and Information Assistant to support our Knowledge and Information Services teams, reporting to the Senior Information Manager and Senior Knowledge Manager.

This role combines two key areas of focus: supporting and assisting the knowledge team with the management and curation of the firm's legal and technical know-how collections - with a focus on AI-enabled curation, innovation and structuring data to drive optimal AI and search outcomes - and providing day-to-day support and assistance to the firm's library and information services, including the maintenance and development of the firm’s hardcopy collection.

## Key responsibilities

The Knowledge and Information Assistant will be required to carry out a broad range of good quality work to support the teams. Key duties will include:

**Knowledge Management**

* assisting with keeping our internal intranet content up to date and answering day-to-day enquiries from the intranet’s content editors to ensure they are posting, editing and tagging correctly so it is optimised for browse, search and AI;
* assisting with the creation and updating of intranet pages and team sites on our enterprise collaboration / content management portals;
* monitoring content / data / taxonomies stored in the firm’s knowledge systems and reporting any discrepancies to help optimise the delivery of high quality and consistent content to the rest of the firm;
* providing input to help improve the rules which facilitate automated / AI-driven processes and classification of legal content;
* supporting the team with quality assurance, e.g. testing new features, workflows etc; and helping to deliver statistical usage reports and analysis of the firm’s knowledge systems;
* assisting with training, new joiner inductions, and communications; and
* creating and updating key documentation, e.g. user guides, FAQs etc to drive engagement with and use of the firm’s knowledge systems.

**Library and Information Services**

* maintaining a tidy and professional appearance of the departmental libraries and the archive, including, shelving books and journals and assisting with periodic stock checks and withdrawal of out-of-date stock;
* managing the circulation of library books, sending out overdue notices to borrowers and checking offices for missing books and journals; assisting with the distribution of permanent loan copies to fee earners;
* filing hardcopy loose-leaf updates and assisting in maintaining the online library management system with accurate records of serials holdings;
* managing the check-in and circulation of periodicals, including receiving and claiming for print journals and maintaining up-to-date circulation lists for both hardcopy and online journals;
* assisting users with requests for journal articles;
* undertaking some basic enquiry work, including legal queries for cases and legislation;
* producing company information reports and research; and
* conducting regular press searching and alerts.

This job description encompasses the main duties of the role and is by no means exhaustive. It is anticipated that duties may vary from time to time according to the needs of the team.

During the first six months of employment, you may be required to attend the office four days per week to support onboarding, training and collaboration. Your line manager may adjust this requirement based on your progress and business needs.

## The candidate

The successful candidate will be committed to providing high-quality support and will thrive on collaborating closely with stakeholders across the business to help drive the delivery of knowledge management and information services projects and programmes. This role suits someone at the start of their career or studying for a postgraduate degree in Library and Information Science, who is seeking to build up their experience across both areas. The individual will be personable with the ability to quickly build trust and confidence with colleagues within the team and across the firm.

The successful candidate will ideally possess the following:

* an undergraduate degree, similar higher education or equivalent experience;
* a qualification in Information/Library Science or currently studying for a similar postgraduate degree;
* an organised, meticulous and methodical approach to work and high attention to detail;
* some experience using AI tools;
* an aptitude for using technology and be highly computer literate, including knowledge of MS Office (Word, Excel and PowerPoint) and database software;
* an awareness of metadata, taxonomies, ontologies and knowledge graphs and how they can be used to classify and structure data;
* being a team player who supports their colleagues and a willingness to participate as part of a small and multitasking team;
* displaying initiative and a pro-active approach to resolving problems; and
* excellent inter-personal communication skills (both written and verbal).

## Application screening

Any offer of employment with us is subject to our pre-employment checks which are conducted by a third-party screening provider. These may include but are not limited to your professional and academic qualifications, any criminal records and employment references. These checks will be initiated with your consent and your offer will be subject to the successful completion of these checks.

## Our commitment to inclusion

Inclusion is one of our key priorities and it is a goal we are actively working towards. We believe that an inclusive, forward-thinking culture is intrinsically important and enables us to provide innovative solutions to our clients.

We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, bringing different perspectives and experiences, making Macfarlanes an exciting and stimulating place to work. We seek to recruit the best candidates, regardless of age, gender, race, ethnicity, social or economic background, religion, disability, sexual orientation or any other characteristic.

As part of this commitment, we will ask you certain diversity data questions. We would really appreciate you and/or your recruiter completing these questions when submitting an application to Macfarlanes as this data enables us to measure our progress and identify any actions needed to continue to support an inclusive culture. This data is anonymised to maintain the privacy of applicants. If you have any questions relating to how this data is used, please contact a member of the recruitment team.

Should you require any adjustments during the application and/or interview process, please do not hesitate to inform your recruiter or a member of the recruitment team. Please note, the job description is available in other accessible formats (for example, large print).

We are a Disability Confident Employer and will offer an interview to disabled applicants who best meet the essential criteria for the role. If you would like to apply through the Disability Confident Interview Scheme, please email the recruitment team at recruitment@macfarlanes.com.

